new file mode 100644
index 0000000..68f81c9
--- /dev/null
+++ b/demos/pause.dem
@@ -0,0 +1,46 @@
+# pause.dem — Story 5.3's launchable golden: pause freezes the sim
+# deterministically; the player plans a fix while frozen; resume continues
+# from the EXACT tick; crises tick only unpaused (the mid-crisis pause).
+#
+# The surge.dem topology (era 3, seed 4243 — crisis-verified): the narrow
+# res->router->host path saturates early and the streaming surge set-piece
+# fires @tick 1200 (= 60000ms): Crisis_Triggered{Surge, Saturated_Bundle} —
+# the banner is up, the surge window (1200..3000) is live. The run PAUSES at
+# 60500ms (tick 1210 — mid-crisis). While paused, the player draws a
+# STANDARD parallel pipe on the 0-1 leg (a paused edit: logged at
+# apply_tick 1211, the next tick the sim will execute — the app's fast-path
+# convention [ODN-2]). RESUME at 70000ms: the sim continues from tick 1211 —
+# the edit lands exactly there, and the crisis state is EXACTLY as paused
+# (no hidden progress — the pause window's 190 wall ticks repeat ONE hash).
+#
+# T1 pins (the "paused state stable" golden): wall ticks 1211..1400 are one
+# repeated FNV-1a-64 hash — the SIM state (flow/crisis/rng/health) is frozen
+# across the pause; the hash changes at 1401 (tick 1211 — the first
+# post-resume step, the logged edit landing exactly there); the replay gate
+# re-sims the blessed log with the SAME schedule and reproduces every hash
+# byte-for-byte (E10). NOTE the model: the harness renders the step-boundary
+# truth (a paused edit applies at the first resumed step); the live app's
+# fast-path shows it immediately while the sim stays frozen — both converge
+# at step boundaries, and fast-path edits are a separate blessed channel
+# (the action log), never a sim-state mutation.
+#
+# T2 captures: 65000ms = the FROZEN crisis frame — the banner up, the narrow
+# pipes still in place (the step-boundary model: the logged edit has not
+# applied yet); 80000ms = post-resume: the parallel standard pipe is in the
+# bundle AND the SAME crisis is still active (the window did not advance
+# during the pause — the crisis banner's countdown is exactly where the
+# pause left it).
+seed 4243
+run 100000ms
+era 3
+fixture off
+spawn_node residential 8 15
+spawn_node router_basic 14 15
+spawn_node content_host 20 15
+at 100ms draw 0 1 narrow
+at 100ms draw 1 2 narrow
+at 60500ms pause
+at 61000ms draw 0 1 standard
+at 70000ms resume
+capture at 65000ms
+capture at 80000ms
